  "raw_meta_yaml": "#\n# See the guidelines for updating this recipe for new releases:\n# https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/wiki/Scrapy-release-procedure#conda-packages\n#\n{% set name = \"Scrapy\" %}\n{% set version = \"2.19.0\" %}\n{% set sha256 = \"34130726582b64c91531162ab277c4053e558876d49ba219cb43679e71d80a87\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name|lower }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  fn: {{ name }}-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  url: https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/source/{{ name[0] }}/{{ name }}/{{ name | lower }}-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: {{ sha256 }}\n\nbuild:\n  script: {{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . --no-deps -vv\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  entry_points:\n    - scrapy = scrapy.cmdline:execute\n\n# The requirements below shall match the requirements from the target package\n# version (check pyproject.toml for changes).\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python {{ python_min }}\n    - pip\n    - hatchling\n\n  run:\n    - python >={{ python_min }}\n    # pywin32 exists for unix as a noop package\n    - pywin32\n\n    # Same order as pyproject.toml:\n    - twisted >=21.7.0\n    - aiohttp >=3.13.3\n    - charset-normalizer >=3.4.0\n    - cryptography >=41.0.5\n    - cssselect >=0.9.1\n    - defusedxml >=0.7.1\n    - itemadapter >=0.1.0\n    - itemloaders >=1.0.1\n    - lxml >=4.6.4\n    - packaging\n    - parsel >=1.5.0\n    - platformdirs >=2.0.0\n    - protego >=0.1.15\n    - pyOpenSSL >=24.3.0\n    - queuelib >=1.6.1\n    - service_identity >=24.2.0\n    - tldextract\n    - w3lib >=2.1.1\n    - zope.interface >=5.1.0\n    - pydispatcher >=2.0.5\n    - brotli-python >=1.2.0\n    # On Python 3.14 and higher the standard library compression.zstd module is\n    # used instead, but a noarch package cannot require this conditionally.\n    - backports.zstd >=1.3.0\n\ntest:\n  requires:\n    - python {{ python_min }}\n    - attrs\n    - botocore\n    - bpython  # [not win]\n    - httpx2\n    - ipython\n    - google-cloud-storage\n    - pip\n    - jmespath\n    - pexpect\n    - pillow\n    - ptpython\n    - pyftpdlib\n    - pytest >=8.4.1\n    - pytest-rerunfailures\n    - pytest-twisted\n    - priority >=1.1.0,<2.0\n    - sybil\n    - setuptools-scm   # required indirectly by pytest-forked\n  source_files:\n    - conftest.py\n    - pyproject.toml\n    - scrapy\n    - tests\n  commands:\n    - scrapy version -v\n    - mv scrapy _scrapy\n    # Scrapy's pyproject.toml turns warnings into errors for environments that\n    # match its own tested dependency versions; -W default opts this\n    # environment out, the same way Scrapy's tox.ini does for its own envs\n    # with different pinned dependencies.\n    # The CI image sets REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE to an empty string, which recent\n    # botocore releases reject outright when creating an S3 client.\n    - unset REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE && pytest _scrapy tests -W default\n\nabout:\n  home: https://scrapy.org/\n  license: BSD-3-Clause-Clear\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: A high-level Python Screen Scraping framework\n  description: |\n    Scrapy is an open source and collaborative framework for extracting the\n    data you need from websites in a fast, simple, yet extensible way.\n  doc_url: https://docs.scrapy.org\n  dev_url: https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - rmax\n    - kmike\n    - Gallaecio\n    - wRAR\n    - dangra\n    - AdrianAtZyte\n",
